It takes a lot of time to locate  data in a magnetic tape, as it is a sequential access medium, similar to an audio cassette. For example, if we need to access the 100th record on the tape, we must first move through the previous 99 records. The capacity of tape media is referred in Terabytes.

Hard disk

The hard disk consists of metal disks coated with magnetic material concealed in dust free containers. Hard disks have very high storage capacity, high data transfer rates and low access time. It is more durable and less error prone. It is the most common secondary storage device used in computers.

A hard disk may contain one or more platters. Each platter requires two read/write heads, one for each surface. A tiny electromagnetic read/write head attached to an access arm magnetises tiny spots on the disk to store data as shown in Figure 2.15. The same electromagnetic head can later sense the magnetic fields of the spots, allowing the data to be read back from the disk.

