8.2 Data communication system

In a computer network, computing devices are connected in various ways, to communicate and share resources. Data communication is the exchange of digital data between any two devices through a medium of transmission. Figure 8.1 show the representation of a general data communication system. The following five basic elements are necessary for building any data communication system.

