This is the most widely used media in small computer networks. It consists of four twisted pairs which are enclosed in an outer shield. These pairs are colour coded. Twisted pair cables are of two types: (i) Unshielded Twisted Pair (UTP) cables and (ii) Shielded Twisted Pair (STP) cables.

